## Do not touch
- Lockfiles by hand, applied migrations, `.env*`, `.github/workflows/`, generated files in `<dir>`

## Working rules
- Think before coding: state assumptions, ask when unclear, surface tradeoffs.
- Simplicity first: the minimum code that solves the task. No speculative features or abstractions.
- Surgical changes: every changed line traces to the request. Mention unrelated problems; do not fix them.
- Goal-driven: turn the task into a check (a failing test, a gate) and loop until it passes.
- No new dependencies or CI changes without asking.
(Working rules paraphrase the principles in the multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills CLAUDE.md, which is MIT-licensed.)
